paragraphs(supp,'''## Supplementary Note 6 New-period and circulation records

The frozen 2020 test plan is stored as operational_test_plan_20261025.md. It was written before retrieval and scoring of the test forecasts. Members 0–10 and the eight domains were fixed in advance. Training origins whose targets extend beyond 2019 are removed. Each prediction metadata file records that verification observations were not loaded during fitting. The primary contrast is H1 minus BU-clim, averaged equally across domains after division by each domain’s training raw CRPS. Circular blocks of four origins give the primary interval; six and eight origins are sensitivity checks. The single verification year permits a new-period test but not inference from independent annual blocks. Historical index revisions and pooled hindcast configurations prevent interpreting this as a reconstruction of real-time operations.

The circulation plan and field checksums accompany the three bounded NetCDF files. Source time coordinates use a 360-day monthly indexing convention; identities from January 2000 through December 2019 are matched without inventing daily timestamps. Wind is in metres per second and specific humidity in kilograms per kilogram, converted to grams per kilogram for presentation. Seasonal means use all available months, and the broad circulation box uses exact cell-overlap area weights. The DJF year convention matches the forecast score grouping by calendar year. The wind–score correlation is exploratory; its interval resamples twenty paired years 50000 times. These monthly 850 hPa fields are not vertically integrated moisture transport or an event-scale MJO attribution.''')
figure(supp,'FigS06_mixtures','Fig. S6. Marginal value of more flexible combinations. State-dependent pooling and inner seasonal selection minus a fixed constant mixture in (a) year-block validation and (b) 2015–2019 forward verification. Hollow squares and bars are paired mean differences and descriptive 95% year-block intervals. Negative values favour the more flexible method.')
figure(supp,'FigS07_forward','Fig. S7. Northern forward verification: (a) annual scores and (b) cross-validation and forward means on the same 2015–2019 years. These periods overlap the development archive. The raw forecast is identical between designs.')
figure(supp,'FigS08_omissions','Fig. S8. All 15504 choices of five omitted years, applied to existing northern annual scores. Panels compare H1 with (a) BU-rain, (b) H0 and (c) BU-clim. These are descriptive distributions of score sensitivity, not sampling distributions or new model fits.')
